  "term": "FBA",
  "definition": "FBA stands for fixel-based analysis, an advanced diffusion MRI method for studying white matter at the level of specific fiber orientations within a voxel. It estimates fiber-specific measures such as fiber density and fiber-bundle shape, helping identify white matter changes, and it typically uses a study-specific population template for group analysis.",
